1
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,719
Just like crying your eyes out,

2
00:00:23,719 --> 00:00:27,320
laughing out loud is also a basic human need.

3
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:33,600
Delivery!

4
00:00:34,479 --> 00:00:35,479
Leave it at the door.

5
00:00:43,039 --> 00:00:43,960
He Jiahuan! Bro Chao!

6
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:45,359
Ow, ow, ow! Bro Chao!

7
00:00:45,399 --> 00:00:46,960
You're ignoring my calls, huh?

8
00:00:46,960 --> 00:00:47,880
No, my phone is on silent.

9
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:49,079
It's always on silent mode.

10
00:00:49,079 --> 00:00:50,479
Didn't you say you had inside info?

11
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:51,679
I slipped up, man.

12
00:00:51,679 --> 00:00:53,560
Buying those stocks cost me 200,000!

13
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:54,840
I... I... I lost money too.

14
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:55,679
You wanna run, huh?

15
00:00:55,679 --> 00:00:57,320
Why... why would I run?

16
00:00:57,439 --> 00:00:58,119
Well...

17
00:00:58,479 --> 00:00:59,320
The money is right inside.

18
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:00,119
I'll go get it for you.

19
00:01:00,439 --> 00:01:01,039
Okay?

20
00:01:01,039 --> 00:01:02,119
Let go, it hurts.

21
00:01:02,119 --> 00:01:04,120
If you dare run today, I'll kill you.

22
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:05,719
No way. It's my house, why would I run?

23
00:01:05,719 --> 00:01:06,359
Bro, come inside.

24
00:01:06,359 --> 00:01:07,879
You guys too. Come in, come in, alright?

25
00:01:08,159 --> 00:01:08,719
I...

26
00:01:08,879 --> 00:01:09,519
After him!

27
00:01:40,359 --> 00:01:41,079
I'm done running.

28
00:01:41,239 --> 00:01:42,000
Hold on, hold on.

29
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:42,879
Wait, wait.

30
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:43,439
No, listen.

31
00:01:43,879 --> 00:01:44,400
No.

32
00:01:44,879 --> 00:01:46,040
Don't come any closer! I, I...

33
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:47,599
I'm calling the police right now!

34
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:48,760
Officer!

35
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:50,000
There's a criminal gang here

36
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:51,319
led by Hu Chaochao.

37
00:01:51,319 --> 00:01:53,439
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven, eight.

38
00:01:53,439 --> 00:01:54,200
They're holding clubs.

39
00:01:54,200 --> 00:01:55,840
Hu as in the surname Hu.

40
00:01:55,959 --> 00:01:58,000
Chao as in Superman. Right.

41
00:01:58,000 --> 00:01:59,280
Come on, call the cops.

42
00:01:59,280 --> 00:01:59,680
Yeah.

43
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:00,760
Let's see if your fraud charge is worse,

44
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:01,439
or my debt collecting.

45
00:02:01,439 --> 00:02:02,120
No, Bro Chao, you...

46
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:03,640
Bro Chao, keep this up and I'll jump!

47
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:04,439
I'll jump!

48
00:02:04,439 --> 00:02:04,920
Jump.

49
00:02:07,359 --> 00:02:07,719
Jump!

50
00:02:07,719 --> 00:02:08,759
No, no, Bro Chao.

51
00:02:08,759 --> 00:02:09,080
Jump!

52
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:10,280
No, Bro Chao, Bro Chao, Bro Chao!

53
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:11,240
Easy now. Go on, jump!

54
00:02:11,479 --> 00:02:12,680
Think jumping gets you out of your debt?

55
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:13,520
I was wrong, bro! I was wrong!

56
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:14,159
Let me tell you,

57
00:02:14,159 --> 00:02:15,800
paying your debts is only right.

58
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:16,800
If you jump, I'll go after your mom.

59
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:17,639
Hear me? Wait, bro.

60
00:02:17,639 --> 00:02:18,439
Bro Chao, I'll...

61
00:02:18,439 --> 00:02:19,240
I... I'll find someone.

62
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,680
I'll pay you back in a couple days.

63
00:02:20,680 --> 00:02:21,800
Just give me two days.

64
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:22,800
I don't have that kind of time. Wait.

65
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:23,479
Wait for you?

66
00:02:23,479 --> 00:02:24,240
Bro, getting a call.

67
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,960
Maybe this is it. The money's here.

68
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:28,719
Speak. I'm busy here.

69
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:29,960
He Jiahuan, where are you?

70
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:31,520
Fang Haowen is going to jump off a building!

71
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:32,800
Is he dead?

72
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:34,520
Not dead. He's trending online.

73
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:35,240
He's jumping right now!

74
00:02:35,240 --> 00:02:36,159
Hold on, hold on, hold on.

75
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:37,400
Okay.

76
00:02:37,680 --> 00:02:38,879
Listen, if you have the time,

77
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:44,680
if you have time to make phone calls right now,

78
00:02:44,879 --> 00:02:47,039
why not borrow some money to save your miserable life?

79
00:02:56,400 --> 00:02:59,080
It's been a while now.

80
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:03,159
I've really wanted to be in a public place

81
00:03:04,599 --> 00:03:06,000
and laugh out loud.

82
00:03:10,360 --> 00:03:11,400
I want to laugh out loud.

83
00:03:14,319 --> 00:03:14,719
If...

84
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,759
If only this were allowed,

85
00:03:17,599 --> 00:03:18,520
how wonderful it would be.

86
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:22,280
Just like sobbing uncontrollably,

87
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:25,680
laughing out loud

88
00:03:27,159 --> 00:03:28,680
is also a basic human need.

89
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:33,759
This is a poem written by Fang Haowen.

90
00:03:34,719 --> 00:03:36,199
I suddenly think he might be talented.

91
00:03:36,199 --> 00:03:38,439
What does his talent have to do with you?

92
00:03:42,719 --> 00:03:43,360
Let's go.

93
00:03:50,240 --> 00:03:52,319
We're going to be rich! Fang Haowen is viral!

94
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:12,120
I hate myself.

95
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:16,040
I hate this world.

96
00:05:19,839 --> 00:05:20,720
Do you remember now?

97
00:05:28,879 --> 00:05:30,240
I wasn't trying to die!

98
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:32,959
I really can't remember.

99
00:05:32,959 --> 00:05:34,560
I drank way too much.

100
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:35,319
As for your situation,

101
00:05:35,319 --> 00:05:36,240
we are aware of it.

102
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:37,959
But I really wasn't trying to jump off a building!

103
00:05:38,399 --> 00:05:40,120
As a success author,

104
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:41,680
you should take my advice.

105
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:43,800
Not bothering others is a kind of success.

106
00:05:44,160 --> 00:05:45,000
Remember that.

107
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:46,560
A miserable life is better than a good death.

108
00:05:47,120 --> 00:05:48,120
Please sign here.

109
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:49,439
Okay.

110
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:53,560
If you need anything, call the police.

111
00:05:53,560 --> 00:05:54,639
Thanks for your trouble.

112
00:05:55,279 --> 00:05:56,120
Thank you so much.

113
00:05:56,120 --> 00:05:57,199
I'm heading out. Keep on living.

114
00:05:57,199 --> 00:05:58,319
Take care. See you.

115
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:04,000
Why are you here?

116
00:06:04,519 --> 00:06:05,439
Why are you so hyped up?

117
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:07,639
And why do you smell like chicken shit?

118
00:06:07,639 --> 00:06:09,199
Shut up. You went viral, you know that?

119
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:10,959
Crazy viral. Super viral.

120
00:06:10,959 --> 00:06:11,759
What do you mean super...

121
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:13,480
Why do you have a chicken feather on your head?

122
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:14,079
Not important.

123
00:06:15,639 --> 00:06:16,319
What are you doing here?

124
00:06:16,319 --> 00:06:17,319
I'm here to take you home.

125
00:06:17,759 --> 00:06:18,439
You're so viral right now,

126
00:06:18,439 --> 00:06:19,439
could you even get home without me?

127
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:20,480
Oh, right.

128
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:21,199
Remember, when we go out later,

129
00:06:21,199 --> 00:06:22,439
don't say anything to the netizens.

130
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:25,000
Try to squeeze out some tears when we exit.

131
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:25,920
Can you manage to cry?

132
00:06:26,439 --> 00:06:28,079
Show them a state of severe depression.

133
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:29,160
That's ridiculous.

134
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:30,319
I don't even have depression.

135
00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:31,879
What's the situation with these netizens?

136
00:06:32,800 --> 00:06:33,439
I what?

137
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:04,399
That's enough. This is a hospital.

138
00:07:04,399 --> 00:07:05,480
Stop filming.

139
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:07,360
Mr. Fang is really depressed.

140
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:08,759
He really needs some privacy.

141
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:09,480
Step aside.

142
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:15,560
Fang Haowen

143
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:17,240
couldn't handle the harsh realities of society,

144
00:07:17,240 --> 00:07:18,519
which triggered his depression.

145
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:25,839
Old Fang,

146
00:07:26,240 --> 00:07:27,959
can you tell me first next time?

147
00:07:27,959 --> 00:07:29,600
What a great opportunity you missed.

148
00:07:30,879 --> 00:07:31,839
What do you mean?

149
00:07:32,399 --> 00:07:33,519
Let me review it for you.

150
00:07:33,759 --> 00:07:34,480
Right now,

151
00:07:34,480 --> 00:07:35,759
haven't you finished your second book?

152
00:07:35,839 --> 00:07:37,319
I'll help you publish your second book.

153
00:07:37,319 --> 00:07:38,480
Taking advantage of this current traffic,

154
00:07:38,839 --> 00:07:41,360
let's do a livestream selling your book.

155
00:07:41,519 --> 00:07:42,399
How much money can it make?

156
00:07:42,399 --> 00:07:43,519
How much can it... How much...

157
00:07:43,519 --> 00:07:44,519
How much money can it make?

158
00:07:46,519 --> 00:07:48,279
I didn't expect so many people to care about my...

159
00:07:49,319 --> 00:07:50,319
underwear.

160
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:51,600
Stop looking at it.

161
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:53,480
We haven't secured that underwear endorsement yet.

162
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:54,920
Old Fang,

163
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,600
let me tell you,

164
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:58,160
things are different for you now.

165
00:07:58,279 --> 00:07:58,839
Don't worry.

166
00:07:58,839 --> 00:08:00,240
Just trust me with that old face of yours.

167
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,680
I'll sell at least 100,000 for you.

168
00:08:02,959 --> 00:08:04,240
Old Fang, don't you look down on...

169
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:06,120
making money.

170
00:08:06,120 --> 00:08:08,040
I'm a scholar. How many times have I said it?

171
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,040
Aren't you guys annoying?

172
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:12,240
Just eat your food.

173
00:08:14,759 --> 00:08:15,560
Old Fang,

174
00:08:17,439 --> 00:08:18,800
you've finally written

175
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:20,040
the second book of your life.

176
00:08:20,279 --> 00:08:22,079
You want to publish it, right?

177
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:24,680
But nobody will publish it for you.

178
00:08:25,399 --> 00:08:26,680
Nobody will publish it for you, Old Fang.

179
00:08:27,199 --> 00:08:28,600
I've calculated if you pay out of pocket.

180
00:08:28,759 --> 00:08:30,680
Including ISBNs, printing...

181
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:31,759
It's at least hundreds of thousands.

182
00:08:32,240 --> 00:08:34,279
You don't have a dime in your pocket.

183
00:08:34,279 --> 00:08:35,759
How are you going to publish it?

184
00:08:36,399 --> 00:08:37,960
Old Fang, let me tell you my strategy.

185
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:39,600
I'll front the money to publish the book.

186
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,320
We'll form a bond.

187
00:08:41,519 --> 00:08:42,639
I'll find a livestream company for you

188
00:08:42,639 --> 00:08:43,399
to Empower you.

189
00:08:43,399 --> 00:08:44,759
Riding on this current heat,

190
00:08:44,759 --> 00:08:46,039
let's Execute this book-selling plan.

191
00:08:46,039 --> 00:08:47,600
Then you can pay me back the publishing money.

192
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:48,519
You have to... you have to pay me back.

193
00:08:48,519 --> 00:08:49,320
The publishing money.

194
00:08:49,399 --> 00:08:51,159
And then, then here's my plan.

195
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:52,679
We'll continue marketing.

196
00:08:54,519 --> 00:08:56,360
We'll continue marketing, stimulate the market,

197
00:08:57,240 --> 00:08:58,159
perfect the logic,

198
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,320
package your New persona,

199
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,919
strengthen netizens' recognition of you.

200
00:09:01,240 --> 00:09:02,840
Let's focus on your scholar attributes.

201
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:03,720
We'll cross-pollinate the categories.

202
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:05,120
We'll keep livestreaming.

203
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,559
We'll raise the dimension,

204
00:09:06,559 --> 00:09:07,559
refine our audience,

205
00:09:07,559 --> 00:09:09,240
and consolidate your business model.

206
00:09:09,240 --> 00:09:10,720
You'll get rich off your talent.

207
00:09:10,720 --> 00:09:11,600
Together, we'll walk

208
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:12,799
the path to the peak of life.

209
00:09:13,159 --> 00:09:14,279
I'm so talented.

210
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:15,399
Old Fang,

211
00:09:15,399 --> 00:09:16,840
can you play any instruments?

212
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:17,759
Besides reciting poetry,

213
00:09:17,759 --> 00:09:19,200
do you have any other talents?

214
00:09:20,559 --> 00:09:22,240
I don't...

215
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:24,159
It's fine, we can package you.

216
00:09:25,600 --> 00:09:26,720
You have a chicken feather on your head.

217
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:28,679
That's not important.

218
00:09:31,440 --> 00:09:32,759
Let me think about it some more.

219
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:34,080
My mind's been a mess these past two days.

220
00:09:34,879 --> 00:09:35,879
I just fell off a building!

221
00:09:35,879 --> 00:09:38,240
Isn't that the perfect fall into place?

222
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:39,639
Stop thinking.

223
00:09:39,720 --> 00:09:40,840
In this information age,

224
00:09:40,840 --> 00:09:42,559
if you don't piggyback on this current traffic,

225
00:09:42,559 --> 00:09:43,840
netizens will forget you in a few days.

226
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,000
If you don't sell your books,

227
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,000
you'll have to jump off the building again in a few days.

228
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,519
Do you believe me? I'll... Wake up!

229
00:09:48,519 --> 00:09:49,639
I'm not asleep.

230
00:09:49,759 --> 00:09:51,840
Fang Haowen, I'll lay it out for you right here.

231
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:52,960
These days, writing non-stop

232
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:54,000
and publishing books is totally useless!

233
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:55,440
You have to promote yourself.

234
00:09:55,879 --> 00:09:57,279
Don't be a lost cause.

235
00:09:58,159 --> 00:09:59,279
If you really want to publish a poetry collection,

236
00:09:59,279 --> 00:10:00,240
come find me tomorrow morning.

237
00:10:00,519 --> 00:10:01,279
If you don't want to,

238
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:02,440
then go jump again.

239
00:10:25,919 --> 00:10:27,320
Driver, I'm going to report you.

240
00:10:27,519 --> 00:10:28,720
Is this even a ride-hailing car?

241
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:29,480
It smells so bad.

242
00:10:29,919 --> 00:10:30,519
Don't you know...

243
00:10:30,519 --> 00:10:31,399
...it's bad for us passengers' health?

244
00:10:31,399 --> 00:10:32,679
Take it off. What are you doing?

245
00:10:32,679 --> 00:10:34,440
Your face mask is totally dried out. Take it off.

246
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:35,240
I'm telling you, if you keep this up...

247
00:10:35,240 --> 00:10:36,240
I'm really going to report you.

248
00:10:48,799 --> 00:10:50,240
Why are my old books still on display?

249
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:52,039
Well, the second book isn't printed yet.

250
00:10:52,039 --> 00:10:54,000
I called the publisher to rush the printing.

251
00:10:54,159 --> 00:10:55,519
We'll do pre-sales first.

252
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:57,320
Once the new book is out,

253
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,639
we'll replace the posters too.

254
00:10:59,200 --> 00:10:59,799
Got it.

255
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:02,799
Mr. Fang!

256
00:11:03,519 --> 00:11:04,840
Mr. Fang! Mr. Fang!

257
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:09,360
This is great, Mr. Fang! Great!

258
00:11:10,519 --> 00:11:13,799
Lei Oulei, CEO of Erma Media.

259
00:11:16,399 --> 00:11:17,519
Hello, hello!

260
00:11:17,519 --> 00:11:18,200
I read your book.

261
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:18,960
I absolutely love it!

262
00:11:18,960 --> 00:11:19,320
Thank you.

263
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:20,159
After finishing your book,

264
00:11:20,159 --> 00:11:21,120
I even became successful!

265
00:11:21,919 --> 00:11:22,399
Thank you.

266
00:11:22,399 --> 00:11:24,240
Which, which chapter do you like specifically?

267
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:26,080
I like every chapter!

268
00:11:30,639 --> 00:11:32,080
Come, come. This way, please.

269
00:11:32,639 --> 00:11:33,799
Our company

270
00:11:33,799 --> 00:11:37,039
is one of the largest livestream platforms in the country.

271
00:11:38,399 --> 00:11:40,080
The highest annual GMV

272
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:41,639
for a single streamer is 120 million.

273
00:11:41,919 --> 00:11:42,720
Last year, our company

274
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:43,639
easily generated a turnover

275
00:11:43,639 --> 00:11:44,759
of 1.4 billion.

276
00:11:45,240 --> 00:11:46,799
Last year, we also effortlessly

277
00:11:46,799 --> 00:11:48,399
trained over 600 streamers.

278
00:11:48,639 --> 00:11:50,080
What you see is just the tip of the iceberg.

279
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:51,080
